{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4527","id":4734085518,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU59Ms88AAAABGixpjg","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4527","diff_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4527.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pull/4527.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4527","number":4527,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"SF-A29-T05.1: isolate bounded parser cases and retain replayable findings","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.com/wieslawsoltes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Task: SF-A29-T05.1\nRelated: #1143, #1151\n\n## Problem and change\n\nProject #4 had no shared execution or retained-corpus implementation for its eight parser targets. This batch composes the adapters merged in #4524 and #4525 with deterministic byte mutations, a disposable child per case, strict time/input/output/memory limits, and hash-checked finding persistence and replay.\n\nOnly a static registry can select the eight reviewed adapters. Input cannot choose a module, executable or callback. Children receive a sanitized environment without ambient Node options or credentials. V8 old space is capped; Linux RSS observations and returned peak RSS are checked. Cancellation, startup/case overruns, abnormal exits, output overflow and unexpected exceptions remain separate findings or incomplete outcomes.\n\nCorpus records retain literal input, its digest, the observed source identity and exact effective budgets. Persistence rejects attempts to relabel any of these. Reads reject altered records, symlinks, excess entries and excess actual bytes. An exclusive writer lock bounds concurrent persistence; replay never widens recorded limits or rewrites original evidence.\n\nFinite harness self-checks exercise deadline, 4 MiB allocation, output and disposal guards in a separate fixed worker. These self-checks cannot be selected by product campaigns.\n\n## Validation\n\n- At local commit `99ec786c7ca504be66801d83c4843b9c517150f1`, `node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/conformance/fuzz/*.test.js`: **68 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** on Node 24.19.0 / Linux x64.\n- The published commit has the identical verified tree `f6619080b4904be549a7762b7ef88686a91e6c6d`. Its commit ID differs because publication used GitHub's Git object API.\n- Separate integrated checkout `07c833a82084b8fc07e4d9263bf83e315998e1ab` passed `npm run check` (3,746 linked modules, zero errors) and production build. Structure checking remained advisory with existing repository violations.\n- A clean-source seed-1 integrated campaign completed 256 cases: 37 accepted, 213 controlled rejections, 6 unsupported, 0 findings. Its aggregate status was **unsupported / qualified=false**, not a parser-safety claim.\n- Required PR core remains the hosted publication gate; ordinary core does not execute the Node suite.\n\n## Scope and remaining work\n\nThis is the reusable runtime/persistence batch. The CLI, retained ordinary-suite discovery, reproduction metadata, manual workflow and coverage documentation follow in the dependent batch. Broader request sequences, workspace import, existing PDB corpus and bounded native-host checks are separate adapter follow-ups.\n\nRSS sampling and V8 limits are not an operating-system memory or network sandbox. No native CLR, Rust/Wasm, Windows/macOS or ten-minute qualification is claimed. Full #1143/#1151 acceptance remains open; no Project fields, existing claim refs or other agents' leased paths were changed.\n\nNo product package changes or dependencies.\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T11:46:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T11:47:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-04T11:47:24Z","merged_at":"2026-10-04T11:47:24Z","merge_commit_sha":"5a74e83d4a576f50c07d1983b3377e20a881924d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":12525232279,"node_id":"LA_kwDOU59Ms88AAAAC6o_glw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/labels/size/XL","name":"size/XL","color":"C32607","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4527/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/4527/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/issues/4527/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wieslawsoltes/SharpForge/statuses/b6a8e503721f1d08489924e9b24f2094f5e8a3f3","head":{"label":"wieslawsoltes:codex/p4-fuzz-runtime","ref":"codex/p4-fuzz-runtime","sha":"b6a8e503721f1d08489924e9b24f2094f5e8a3f3","user":{"login":"wieslawsoltes","id":2297442,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTc0NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2297442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wieslawsoltes","html_url":"https://github.co